sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Dev as Developer Browser
    participant API as FastAPI Server
    participant Reg as Cancel Registry
    participant Orch as ScanOrchestrator
    participant ChkA as Plugin Check A
    participant ChkB as Plugin Check B
    participant DB as SQLAlchemy DB

    Note over Orch,ChkB: Scenario 1 - Per-Check Error Isolation
    Orch->>ChkA: run(check_context) inside try/except boundary
    ChkA--xOrch: Raises ReadTimeout or Unexpected Exception
    Orch->>Orch: Catch exception, log structured error, record warning
    Orch-->>API: Emit SSE event check_warning (check_id, error_type)
    API-->>Dev: SSE data non-fatal warning badge (scan continues)

    Orch->>ChkB: run(check_context)
    ChkB-->>Orch: Returns List of RawFinding
    Orch->>DB: Commit enriched findings from Check B
    Orch-->>API: Emit SSE event finding_discovered

    Note over Dev,DB: Scenario 2 - Cooperative User Cancellation
    Dev->>API: POST /api/scans/{id}/cancel
    API->>Reg: Lookup threading.Event for scan_id and call cancel_event.set()
    API-->>Dev: 202 Accepted (cancellation_requested=true)

    Orch->>Reg: Poll cancel_event.is_set() before next probe or check
    Reg-->>Orch: True (stop signal active)
    Orch->>Orch: Halt active probing and preserve committed findings
    Orch->>Orch: Recompute partial risk_score from committed findings
    Orch->>DB: UPDATE scans SET status=cancelled, finished_at=now
    Orch->>Reg: Unregister cancel_event(scan_id)
    Orch-->>API: Emit SSE event scan_cancelled
    API-->>Dev: SSE data status=cancelled, partial_findings_preserved=true
